    "body": "The W3C Web Annotation Working Group finished some standards that, among other things, attempt to codify [generic selectors for documents](https://www.w3.org/TR/annotation-model/#selectors). It has some buy in from ebook/article publishers; it’s being used for annotations targeting specific selections by the Web Publishing Group, which is the successor to the people who governed ePub. Might be worth a look for you.\r\n\r\nAs for elaborating URL fragment selectors, The WHATWG has pretty strict criteria for adding any new proposals to HTML itself.  Take a look at [WHATWG Working Mode](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#new-proposals). It suggests that new proposals are incubated separately from the HTML Standard. Many such new proposals are incubating in the [WICG](https://wicg.io), which encourages proposals and feedback from web developers in general. You might have more luck posting this in WICG and soliciting support from the community and from browser vendors there. ",
